  "query_preview": "../Saturday through Monday/... Drier weather is expected \ninto the weekend as offshore flow will become predominate Saturday \ninto Sunday with high pressure beginning to build over the gulf. \nLate Friday into Saturday, a low pressure system will quickly move \nsouth of the panhandle. This, along with high pressure over the \nYukon, will increase the pressure gradient which in turn will \nincrease wind speeds. Strongest wind speeds will most likely be \nacross the northern inner channels, including Taku Inlet, with \nnortherly winds around 20 kts possible. The low pressure system to \nthe south still looks to be on the weaker side which could prevent \nwinds getting any stronger. Because of this weak outflow, low \novernight temperatures will continue to drop. This will bring low \ntemperatures into the 30s with the northern panhandle, becoming more \nlikely to see lows in the mid to high 20s overnight. At the end of \nthe weekend, a weak short wave will slightly increase precipitation \nchances over the northern gulf coast. Any precipitation amounts will \nremain on the lighter side with little to no forecasted \naccumulation amounts.",
